The maintainer's abuild public keys live here: one .rsa.pub a key,
committed, so mkapk.sh --release can prove the key that signed an .apk
is the maintainer's and not a throwaway. Never a private half: a file
ending in .rsa (without .pub) is refused by CI, and the private key
itself lives only offline with the maintainer (or, at release time,
in a CI secret). No key is committed yet. Setup, fingerprints and
rotation are in doc/release-signing.md.
